.systems/ai/core/execution-modes.md:37:The optional `execution-readiness.template.json` projection is inspected by `check-execution-modes --state <file>`. It contains declared unit prerequisites, work kind, decisions, approved actions, baseline and exclusive resources. The pure inspector computes readiness, transitive blocking and completion. Planning units allow only artifact-write, formal-quality and local-commit actions; read-only units reject write actions. Unknown action names are rejected. High-impact agent choices require scoped approval references for all affected units. It performs no writes, launches or approval verification. A declared reference or true flag is not proof: the coordinator must verify real sources, gates, repository baseline and resource isolation before execution. An unknown or malformed projection is rejected.
.systems/ai/core/autopilot.md:167:- Verify recorded human approval for high-risk work; a concrete accepted plan may already cover its named local implementation and formal Quality. Critical-risk and newly uncovered effects retain required human approval.
.systems/ai/core/parallel-task-orchestration.md:3:Execution modes under execution-modes.md are inherited by workers from one coordinator. A queued decision blocks affected units, dependents and shared reservations; verified independent units may continue. Local plan approval may already cover named high-risk Quality; check the actual source at the gate without repeating approval requests.
